From: DuDuClaw OS Y6-1 (2026-08-26)
Subject: log.cpp: fmt::localtime() was removed from fmt's public API

Real do_compile failure caught building fcitx5 5.1.12 against oe-core's
pinned fmt 12.1.0 (openembedded-core/meta/recipes-devtools/fmt/
fmt_12.1.0.bb): "error: 'localtime' is not a member of 'fmt'". fcitx5
5.1.12 predates fmt's removal of the fmt::localtime()/fmt::gmtime() public
helpers -- confirmed by grepping the actual staged
include/fmt/chrono.h that this build produces (no `localtime` symbol
anywhere in it), not by trusting fmt's changelog alone. fmt still supports
formatting a plain std::tm directly via its own
`formatter<std::tm, Char>` specialization (same header, unchanged), so
this computes the std::tm with the same POSIX thread-safe conversion
(localtime_r) fmt::localtime used internally.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet submitted to fcitx/fcitx5]
Signed-off-by: DuDuClaw OS Y6-1

--- a/src/lib/fcitx-utils/log.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/fcitx-utils/log.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 
 #if FMT_VERSION >= 50300
 #include <chrono>
+#include <ctime>
 #include <fmt/chrono.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -222,7 +223,17 @@
             auto floor = std::chrono::floor<std::chrono::seconds>(now);
             auto micro = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(
                 now - floor);
-            auto t = fmt::localtime(std::chrono::system_clock::to_time_t(now));
+            // fmt::localtime() was removed from fmt's public API in
+            // newer fmt releases -- confirmed absent from fmt 12.1.0's
+            // actual staged include/fmt/chrono.h (oe-core's pinned fmt
+            // version), not inferred from a changelog. fmt still formats a
+            // plain std::tm directly via its own formatter<std::tm, Char>
+            // specialization (same header, still present in 12.1.0), so
+            // this computes the std::tm with the POSIX thread-safe
+            // conversion fmt::localtime used internally anyway.
+            std::time_t tt = std::chrono::system_clock::to_time_t(now);
+            std::tm t{};
+            localtime_r(&tt, &t);
             auto timeString = fmt::format("{:%F %T}.{:06d}", t, micro.count());
             out_ << timeString << " ";
         } catch (...) {
